.TH elfshaker-esi-create 1  "elfshaker 1.0.0-rc1" "elfshaker Manual"
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-esi\-create \- Creates an empty ESI index
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker esi create\fR <\fB\-\-meta\fR> <\fB\-\-url\fR> [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-backup\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIesi_file\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Creates an empty ESI index
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-meta\fR
Wire\-format version to write.
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
v1
.IP \(bu 2
v2
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-url\fR
Public URL recorded in the index.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Replace an existing ESI file.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-backup\fR
Do not replace <ESI_FILE>.bak with the previous contents.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Show informational progress and diagnostic messages.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR \fI<PATH>\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Use PATH as the data directory containing packs, indexes, loose objects, remotes, and HEAD. This does not change the working directory.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIesi_file\fR>
ESI file to create.
